<article class="env-lemma" id="0DV2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DV2">Lemma <span data-tag="0DV2">59.51.10</span>.</a> Let $I$ be a directed set. Let $g_ i : X_ i \to S_ i$ be an inverse system of morphisms of schemes over $I$. Assume $g_ i$ is quasi-compact and quasi-separated and for $i' \geq i$ the transition morphisms $X_{i'} \to X_ i$ and $S_{i'} \to S_ i$ are affine. Let $g : X \to S$ be the limit of the morphisms $g_ i$, see Limits, Section <a href="/tag/01YV" data-tag="01YV">32.2</a>. Denote $f_ i : X \to X_ i$ and $h_ i : S \to S_ i$ the projections. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an abelian sheaf on $X$. Then we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  R^ pg_*\mathcal{F} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits _{i \in I} h_ i^{-1}R^ pg_{i, *}(f_{i, *}\mathcal{F})  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Formal combination of Lemmas <a href="/tag/0EYM" data-tag="0EYM">59.51.8</a> and <a href="/tag/0EYN" data-tag="0EYN">59.51.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>